* Arthur Alinovi <aalinovi@riseup.net> [2025-03-03 07:32]:
> I started using rmail yesterday and am trying to figure out how to
> send html mail.
> 
> If I attach an html file and then use M-x mml-insert part and choose
> text/html what I get is 2 lines reading:
> <#part type="text/html" disposition=inline>
> <#/part>
> followed by the attached message.
> 
> If I send it lke that I just get the raw html.
> The only way to format the mail properly is to delete that <#/part>
> line and insert it at the end of the email.
> 
> Is this the proper way to do it or am I doing something wrong?

There must be a way to go, but if Rmail can provide multipart/mixed, that is the question.

First this line must exist somewhere:

Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="=_your.example.com-1086685-1711109692-0001-2"

  
  --=_your.example.com-1086685-1711109692-0001-2
  Content-Type: text/html; name="Insaatproductsview.html"; charset=utf-8
  Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64
  Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="Insaatproductsview.html"
  
and that one. 

Try changing disposition to "attachment", maybe it starts working. 
-- 
Jean Louis

